beads.body:
Add legalityCheck() to plant/production.mjs: today a structurally illegal network (fan-out, a cycle, an edge with no shared resource or an ambiguous one, an unknown node kind, a duplicate id, a non-positive rate/demand/capacity, a processor with zero inputs or outputs) is only reported as a THROWN exception from feasible() — every one of those cases is already pinned in plant/test/production.selftest.mjs's throws() checks, but nothing in this tree can show a visitor WHICH reason fired without wrapping feasible() in a try/catch and parsing a developer-console error message. LEVEL_1 and this turn's other proposal (LEVEL_2) only ever exercise the QUANTITATIVE refusal path (feasible-but-short); the STRUCTURAL refusal path (illegal wiring) has zero player-legible surface. This is deliberately backend-only prerequisite work for a future 'wire it wrong' level, and it does not touch index.html or level-view.js, so it cannot collide with the other proposal in this turn.

Bounded paths: plant/production.mjs (add one new export, do not touch feasible/band/analyse's existing behaviour), plant/test/legality.selftest.mjs (new, createsGate).

plant/production.mjs already defines (but does not export) analyse({ nodes, edges }), which throws Error with a distinct message per cause. Add a second, non-throwing entry point around that SAME internal function, additive only:
  export function legalityCheck(network) {
    try { analyse(network); return { legal: true, reason: null }; }
    catch (e) { return { legal: false, reason: e.message }; }
  }
Do not change analyse's throw sites, do not change feasible()'s signature or its own throwing behaviour — plant/test/production.selftest.mjs's throws(() => feasible(...)) assertions are the existing pin for every one of these causes and must keep passing without that file being touched at all.

Gate (plant/test/legality.selftest.mjs, does not exist yet — create it): import legalityCheck and feasible from '../production.mjs'. Reuse the exact fixture objects already in plant/test/production.selftest.mjs's 'fan-out and cycles', 'resource matching' and 'other refusals' sections (copy them in, do not import test-from-test) and for each assert legalityCheck(fixture).legal === false and .reason is a string containing the keyword production.mjs's own Error message already uses for that cause (e.g. 'fan-out', 'cycle', 'no shared resource', 'ambiguous', 'unknown node kind', 'duplicate id'). Assert legalityCheck on a plain valid source->processor->sink fixture (reuse production.selftest.mjs's first case) and on plant/levels/level1.mjs's LEVEL_1 both return { legal: true, reason: null }. Finally, using the same throws() helper pattern as production.selftest.mjs, assert feasible() still throws on every one of those illegal fixtures — a direct regression check that this ticket did not change feasible()'s contract. Must also still pass unmodified: node plant/test/production.selftest.mjs.
